{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I understand the pattern. I need to:\n1. Create build scripts for both CSVs under `.xorq/scripts/`\n2. Build them into `.xorq/builds`\n3. Add them to the catalog one at a time\n4. Then compose a metric that calculates farmers markets per 100,000 residents\n5. Verify the answer\n\nSince this is a cross-dataset metric (farmers markets from one source, population from another), I should follow the \"cross-dataset ratio pattern\" which means creating a single build script that reads both sources and joins them.\n\nActually, looking at the data:\n- First source: US farmers markets by state, need total excluding territories\n- Second source: Census data with 2025 population for the United States\n\nThis is trickier because I need:\n- A simple total from the farmers markets table\n- One specific row from the census table (the United States row)\n\nThis matches the \"No shared key\" pattern: \"a whole-table total against a single reference row.\"\n\nLet me create a build script that:\n1. Reads the farmers markets CSV\n2. Reads the census CSV\n3. Filters the census to just \"United States\"\n4. Aggregates farmers markets to get the total (excluding territories)\n5. Joins them and calculates the metric\n\nBut first, I need to ingest both raw sources separately to inspect their schemas. Let me do that.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Now I'll ingest both data sources. Let me create build scripts for each CSV."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01J1GFNKXpBEpsZr6CWFxamp","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"mkdir -p .xorq/scripts"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":13,"output":401,"cacheRead":8719,"cacheWrite":4744,"totalTokens":13877,"cost":{"input":0.000013,"output":0.0020050000000000003,"cacheRead":0.0008719000000000001,"cacheWrite":0.00593,"total":0.0088199},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":319},"stopReason":"