{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_end","contentIndex":2,"toolCall":{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01PZxhpNTNwX4aNp7CPGSBqH","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/private/tmp/trial-pi-41-fvvypi6d/.xorq/scripts/build_farmers_markets_per_capita.py","content":"import urllib.request as u\n_o = u.build_opener()\n_o.addheaders = [(\"User-Agent\", \"Mozilla/5.0\")]\nu.install_opener(_o)\n\nfrom xorq.vendor.ibis.common.collections import FrozenDict\nimport xorq.api as xo\n\nso = FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0\"})\ncon = xo.pandas.connect()\n\n# Read farmers markets data\nfact = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    con,\n    table_name=\"farmers_markets\",\n    storage_options=so,\n)\n\n# Read census population data\nref = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    con,\n    table_name=\"census\",\n    storage_options=so,\n)\n\n# Filter out territories from farmers markets (exclude PR, VI, GU, AS, MP, UM)\n# and sum total farmers markets\nterritories = [\"PR\", \"VI\", \"GU\", \"AS\", \"MP\", \"UM\"]\nfact_filtered = fact.filter(~fact.state_abbr.isin(territories))\ntotal_markets = fact_filtered.aggregate(total_markets=fact_filtered.farmers_markets.sum()).mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n\n# Filter census to just United States row and extract 2025 population\nus_pop = ref.filter(ref.NAME == \"United States\").select(\"POPESTIMATE2025\").mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n\n# Join and calculate metric\nexpr = (\n    total_markets.join(us_pop, total_markets.k == us_pop.k)\n    .mutate(markets_per_100k=total_markets.total_markets / us_pop.POPESTIMATE2025 * 100000)\n    .select(\"total_markets\", \"POPESTIMATE2025\", \"markets_per_100k\")\n)\n"}}}}
{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! I can see that there are territories in the data: PR (Puerto Rico) and VI (Virgin Islands). The user asked for \"total farmers markets (excl. territories)\", so I should exclude PR and VI (and any other territories if present). \n\nThe main US states and DC are included. Territories would be PR, VI, GU, AS, MP, UM - but in this table I only see PR and VI. Let me be safe and exclude all known territories: PR, VI, GU, AS, MP, UM.\n\nActually, looking at the full list, I see PR and VI at the end. Those are the territories. Let me create a build script that:\n1. Gets the total farmers_markets from all rows except territories (PR, VI, GU, AS, MP, UM)\n2. Gets the population from census where NAME == \"United States\"\n3. Calculates farmers_markets / population * 100000\n\nLet me create this as a derived metric following the cross-dataset pattern.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Now let me create a build script that calculates the metric - farmers markets per 100,000 residents (excluding territories):"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01PZxhpNTNwX4aNp7CPGSBqH","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/private/tmp/trial-pi-41-fvvypi6d/.xorq/scripts/build_farmers_markets_per_capita.py","content":"import urllib.request as u\n_o = u.build_opener()\n_o.addheaders = [(\"User-Agent\", \"Mozilla/5.0\")]\nu.install_opener(_o)\n\nfrom xorq.vendor.ibis.common.collections import FrozenDict\nimport xorq.api as xo\n\nso = FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0\"})\ncon = xo.pandas.connect()\n\n# Read farmers markets data\nfact = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    con,\n    table_name=\"farmers_markets\",\n    storage_options=so,\n)\n\n# Read census population data\nref = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    con,\n    table_name=\"census\",\n    storage_options=so,\n)\n\n# Filter out territories from farmers markets (exclude PR, VI, GU, AS, MP, UM)\n# and sum total farmers markets\nterritories = [\"PR\", \"VI\", \"GU\", \"AS\", \"MP\", \"UM\"]\nfact_filtered = fact.filter(~fact.state_abbr.isin(territories))\ntotal_markets = fact_filtered.aggregate(total_markets=fact_filtered.farmers_markets.sum()).mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n\n# Filter census to just United States row and extract 2025 population\nus_pop = ref.filter(ref.NAME == \"United States\").select(\"POPESTIMATE2025\").mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n\n# Join and calculate metric\nexpr = (\n    total_markets.join(us_pop, total_markets.k == us_pop.k)\n    .mutate(markets_per_100k=total_markets.total_markets / us_pop.POPESTIMATE2025 * 100000)\n    .select(\"total_markets\", \"POPESTIMATE2025\", \"markets_per_100k\")\n)\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":13,"output":898,"cacheRead":19256,"cacheWrite":617,"totalTokens":20784,"cost":{"input":0.000013,"output":0.00449,"cacheRead":0.0019256000000000002,"cacheWrite":0.00077125,"total":0.007199850000000001},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":228},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786912061370,"responseId":"msg_011Ce74HwRSnBu1xcCpp6JVQ","rawStopReason":"tool_use"}}
